==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|iːtə(ɹ)|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To tilt back and forth on an edge.
#: ''Adjust the feet if you can '''teeter''' the washing machine.''
# {{context|figuratively}} To be [[indecisive]].
#: ''We '''teetered''' on the fence about buying getaway tickets and missed the opportunity.''
# {{context|figuratively}} To be close to becoming a typically negative situation.
#: ''In truth, the firm was '''teetering''' on the edge of bankruptcy.''

